WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Sometimes, otherworlders come to this world.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.670
Called the "Lost Ones," they possess special,

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.500
powerful abilities that have the potential
to distort the shape of the world itself,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.790
known as Pure Concepts.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:21.040
My job is to dispose of them before their
power has an impact on our world.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.250
I'm a priestess: pure, just, and strong...

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.500
as well as an Executioner for exterminating Lost Ones.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.290
According to Momo's information,
the target is in that building over there.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.580
It's guarded heavily, as expected.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.750
I could take them out,
but I don't want to cause a commotion if at all possible.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.000
This outfit has been quite handy.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.170
It's good for hiding my scripture, too. Good work, Momo.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.540
I thought this might happen,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.630
so I made this beforehand
with plenty of love in every stitch!

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.040
Although I do think she put a bit too much effort into it.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.130
This should do it.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.080
<b><i>Invoke</i></b>

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.540
<b><i>Thread</i></b>

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.420
She's the other Lost One.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.750
The target I must execute tonight.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.830
<b>Episode 2: The Lost One</b>

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.000
Are you the girl who came from another world?

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:18.920
Uh, yes!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:20.420
I see...

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.000
Thank goodness!
What school and class are you from?

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.960
Nishibori High School, Class 1-3.
My name is Akari Tokitou.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.290
Based on her answer, this girl's definitely my target.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.880
Akari. Got it. I'm Menou.
I'm one of the Faust, of the first class.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.630
"F-Faust"?

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:38.960
We can't let them see us.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:39.880
Come inside.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.710
Let's get you out of here, Akari.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.080
Uh... What?!

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.380
Listen, Akari...

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.130
I heard about you from the other one.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.500
"Other one"?

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.830
There was a boy who got summoned
from Japan the same time you were.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:59.920
He found out what the Noblesse,
the ones who summoned you, were up to and ran away.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:05.630
He came to my church for refuge,
but he was injured so badly I couldn't save him.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:06.750
What?

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.330
But he still told me about you before he died.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.080
That's why I want to save you, at least!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:17.580
I know this story's full of holes,
but I can't give her time to think.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.710
They said you have some kind of power, didn't they?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.630
Y-yeah...

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.130
Apparently it's a power that can heal people's wounds.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.210
The Noblesse plan to abuse that power.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:32.080
Even if it's a power for healing,
they'll definitely find a way to use it for no good.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.460
That's why we have to run. Right away!

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.750
I'm on your side, Akari.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.420
Okay, I believe you.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.630
They said you have some kind of power, didn't they?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.080
Y-yeah...

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.880
Apparently it's a power that can heal people's wounds.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.130
It sounds like her power isn't an aggressive one.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.670
Then now's my chance,
while she still has her guard down.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.630
Wait, what? Menou...?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.080
<b><i>Pure Concept [Time]</i></b>

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.290
<b><i>Invoke [Regression]</i></b>

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.920
O-oooh, ow...

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.130
I-I think I tripped or something.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.540
Oh. Hey, Menou!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.670
Her wound disappeared?!

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.790
I'm sorry I'm such a clutz!
Did she heal it? No, that's not it. It's not just the wound.<b></b>

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.710
We have to hurry and get out of here, right?
The bloodstains disappeared, too.<b></b>

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.210
What is this? What is her power?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.960
<i>Could it be... the Pure Concept of Time?</i>

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.380
Menou?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.080
Momo!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.040
Yes?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.830
I'm taking the Lost One with me!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.250
What do you mean? Didn't you kill her on the spot?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:55.080
I'll explain properly later.
Go disrupt the guards on the east side!

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.670
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.040
I don't like the sound of this.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.920
Hello there, stupid Noblesse! I'm a suspicious intruder!

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.790
An intruder! Get her!

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.750
We need to make a run for it, Akari!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.250
Wh-what are we going to do, Menou?!

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.920
Uh, what?!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:17.960
Menou-?!

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.880
Her Pure Concept won't let her die?

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:42.380
Yes, it's impossible to kill her with what I have on hand.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.000
And you're sure her power isn't
"healing" but "time regression"?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.420
Absolutely.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:51.670
The Pure Concept that improperly attached
<i>to her soul is most definitely that of Time.</i><b></b>

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.790
That's a problem.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:08:00.250
<i>All Pure Concepts have disastrous potential, but Time...</i>

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.210
Yes.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:07.170
It might only revive her through regression for now,
but who knows how it will develop if it grows stronger?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.750
The more one uses a Pure Concept,

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:16.250
the more it will eat away at the mind before
eventually taking over and raging out of control.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:21.630
If her Pure Concept were to grow
stronger and get out of control...

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.250
The Sword of Salt that melted the
western continent into the sea.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:28.420
The Pandemonium that devoured
the southernmost archipelago.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:32.040
The Material Room that took over the
Wild Frontier in the east.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:36.040
The Starhusk that carved out the center of
the northern continent and set it afloat.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:41.040
Her power could cause a catastrophe worse
than even the Four Major Human Errors.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.540
What should we do?

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.290
Don't worry.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:48.040
Bring the otherworlder with you to where I am.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.040
What? To Garm?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.040
We have here...

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.920
a ceremonial hall that can eliminate any otherworlder.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:09:00.210
Although we only use it in cases where
the Executioners can't manage.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:03.130
Embarrassingly, I never knew of its existence.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:10.630
Your Master Flare never once relied on my help,
so I assume she never told you, either.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.540
Bring the otherworlder to me.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:17.460
It will take me about three days to get the hall ready,
so get here by then.

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.080
Understood.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.460
I'm grateful for the depth of your wisdom
and consideration, Archbishop.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.670
I could do so much better, though.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:31.920
Lately, there have been a series of young
women disappearing here in Garm.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:36.750
I hate to think that I can't even save
the people who are within my reach.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.830
Oh, but listen to me complain. I'm sorry.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:44.130
Once you get to Garm,
let us have a nice long chat, Miss Menou.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.880
<b>The Lord is watching</b>

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.750
Akari! Get up!

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.710
Wow!

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.580
Thank you, Menou!

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.960
Don't mind if I do!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.330
Oh, you use chopsticks here.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.460
Akari, keep eating and listen.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.460
The Noblesse are definitely going to come after you.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.710
This church isn't safe by any means.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.500
Yeah, this church looks like it's about to fall down.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.960
Like I explained earlier,

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.170
Lost Ones like you have special
powers we call "Pure Concepts,"

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.040
and that's what the Noblesse are after.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.500
Hey, these omelet thingies are really good!
Can I have seconds?

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:29.170
Th-there aren't any more!

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.290
Look, Akari.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:34.130
Even just the bodies of Lost Ones
can be used as magecraft material.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.880
Some won't care if you're dead if
they can get their hands on you!

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.250
What, really? That's scary.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.500
Right? That's why I'm thinking of relocating.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:48.380
We're going to go to the ancient capital of Garm,
where our Church's cathedral is.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.040
Ooh, a journey!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.460
You and me,
setting off on a riveting adventure of escape!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:59.880
What special feelings will develop between
the two along their lengthy journey?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:04.750
It sounds like you're imagining something epic,
but it's just half a day and a bit by railroad.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:06.580
What? Where's the romance in that?

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.380
<i>That's what you're complaining about?</i>

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:09.920
Anyway in Garm,

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:15.080
there's actually a ceremonial hall that can
be used to send otherworlders back home!

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.920
Then that means... I'm going back to Japan?

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.290
Exactly.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:24.750
I spoke to the archbishop in Garm,
so you'll be able to go back in no time.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:25.920
I see!

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:26.750
That's right!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:29.920
But...

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:31.830
What's wrong?

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:37.920
I don't know.
I'm not sure why, but I suddenly felt really sad.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.920
When I first met you, Menou,

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.540
I was startled of course,

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:48.250
but more than that it made me really, really, happy.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:48.830
What?

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.750
I don't really understand it, either,
but for some reason it felt like...

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:56.330
time had started moving again after a long pause.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:00.380
That the moment I'd been waiting for had finally arrived.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:03.790
Wait, what? What's wrong with me?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.880
You must think I'm really odd.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:10.630
But Menou, I'm glad I got to come to this world.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:13.130
I'm so glad I got to meet you.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.170
You know what it is?

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:18.080
I'm pretty sure this is that thing they call fate!

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:27.380
When you put it that way,
I've got to say it feels pretty nice.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:32.130
It should take a few days to prepare the ceremony,
so we can spend a bit more time together.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:34.170
I hope we can be friends, Akari.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.580
Uh-huh! I hope so too, Menou!

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.460
Here's the report.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:57.380
They're going to officially put
King Grisarika on trial for heresy.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.170
They'll begin as early as this afternoon.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.080
I see.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:05.040
This will make it hard for the Noblesse to do anything.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:06.170
That's good for us.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:07.250
Other than that,

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:13.420
seeing the breakfast I prepared for you chowed down
by Miss Boobalicious in there was really infuriating.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:15.500
No one asked you to comment on that.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.710
Let's just make quick work of her now!

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:23.420
It's true direct attacks might not do anything,
but what if we poison her gradually by-

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.380
No.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.170
That might destroy her mind.

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:31.330
That kind of attack on someone possessing
a Pure Concept is taboo.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.290
A Pure Concept is instable enough as it is.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.710
There'll be a higher risk of it getting out of control.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.540
I know that, but...

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:44.170
Repeated revival through regression is enough for
the Pure Concept to develop into a greater risk.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:48.460
That's why we can't try killing her in
ways that don't have good odds.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.290
All right?

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.170
Fine.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.880
So, did you get what I asked for?

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.710
For starters, I have clothes and stuff in here.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.630
And here are the railroad tickets.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>Express Train Third Class Ticket</b>

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>From Grisarika Central Station</b>

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>to Garm Station</b>

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>Express Train Second Class Ticket</b>

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>From Grisarika Central Station</b>

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:58.670
<b>to Garm Station</b>

00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.670
Thank y-

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.500
Momo?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:07.290
Didn't I say your job was to remain
here and join in on the trial?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.630
I'd rather die first!

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:13.420
In case something happens,
it will be better if Akari doesn't know you exist.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.380
You realize that, don't you?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.830
If it means leaving you alone with the likes of her,

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:24.000
I'd rather kill King Grisarika and force the trial
to end so that I can catch up with you!

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.710
Oh come on, Momo.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.540
That girl is dangerous!

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:33.130
My instinct is blaring sirens that I should
never leave the two of you alone together!

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:35.790
Hey, I know how dangerous that girl could b-

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:37.750
No, you don't understand at all!

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:45.710
You've never had to spend significant
time with a target before, you know?

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.290
That's true, but-

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:50.670
I don't think you're suited for that kind of thing.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:53.040
So I want you to trade places with me!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.170
Starting now, just leave her up to me-

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:55.710
I can't.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.000
Why not?!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.210
"Why"...?

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:03.790
To have to kill someone who hasn't
violated a taboo or committed a crime,

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.040
who's just an ordinary, nice person...

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.880
That's my job. That's why.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.040
Then here's what I'll do.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:17.290
I'll tag along stealthily so that
Boobalicious doesn't notice.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.000
Momo!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.920
I'm coming, and that's final!

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.290
Okay, fine...

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.210
Just make sure you don't run into her by accident.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.880
Honestly, you're way too worried about this, Momo.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:36.540
I'm only going to be with Akari for a few days.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.420
I won't give myself away.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:50.330
I'm not worried about you giving yourself away.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.500
Hey, Menou! You're back!

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.330
Menou?

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.000
Sorry for the wait, Akari.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.210
I went and got some clothes for you.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:14.790
Something's going on at the castle,
and there aren't many guards around right now.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.080
We'll set off as soon as you're changed.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.040
Okay!

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.580
Ooh.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:22.750
Whoa.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.130
Wow!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.830
When you said "station,"
I imagined the ones in Japan,

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.460
but this is much more exciting than I thought!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.000
I feel like a tourist!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.920
I'm glad you're happy with it.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.040
It's so pretty! What is this stuff?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.750
They're particles of etheric light.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.750
The trains in this world run on ether.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.790
"Ether"?

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:45.420
Yes.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:48.130
Ether, the guiding force.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:50.630
<b>Ether</b>

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.580
It's the foundation of our world's civilization.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.460
It's generated from people's souls as well,

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.040
but there are larger sources like
earthen veins and heavenly veins.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:01.170
It's also the power that drives magecraft.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.330
<b>Magecraft</b>

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:04.580
"Magecraft"? Is that like magic?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.170
I think it's a little different.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:10.670
Magecraft is a type of technology,
for controlling and composing ether.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.750
Does that mean anyone can use it?

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.130
Theoretically, yes.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:18.790
But you need specialized tools and training,
and above all, a talent for it.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:21.580
Statistically, there are more people who can't use it.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:26.670
Akari, your ability to use magecraft without tools
or training makes you a special kind of genius.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.960
A "genius"?! Wow, I'm a genius?!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.580
Don't get carried away, now.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.080
Listen, Akari...

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.500
Don't be careless about using magecraft.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.830
People are after you right now.
You can't do anything that attracts attention.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.290
All right. I hear you, Miss Menou.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.000
I'll buy us something to eat on the way.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.500
An extravagant boxed lunch or something would be nice.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.880
I don't have the money for that.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:52.960
Aww!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.210
Mommy!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.790
Mommy?!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:06.250
Are you lost?

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:08.630
Are you okay?

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:10.500
Yup.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:14.290
What a good girl! You're not crying! So strong!

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.710
Oh, you scraped your palm.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.580
Let's see...

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.170
Here's your change.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:23.960
Thank you.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.830
Knights from the castle?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.330
Are they looking for Akari?

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.130
No, that's unlikely.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:36.290
They seem to be looking for something,
but they don't have a sense of urgency.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.670
As long as we stay inconspicuous until they're gone...

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.710
Now, let's make that owie...

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.130
Akari!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:46.630
If she uses that magecraft now,
she'll attract their attention!

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:48.500
<b><i>Invoke</i></b>

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.500
<b><i>Bubble</i></b>

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.170
What's this?!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.170
Who would do this in here?

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.250
Is it a prank?

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.790
What's going on?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.460
So pretty!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.790
Take that!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.380
Menou, what's with the karate chop?

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:09.130
I told you not to attract attention, didn't I?!

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:09.790
What?

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.250
It's okay, these bubbles are getting all the attention.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.580
I'll have you know I had to make these myself!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.790
What?! You did this, Menou?!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.210
You shouldn't attract attention with magecraft!

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:20.170
Don't give me that!

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.000
Hey.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:24.580
Did you make these, Miss? You're amazing!

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.580
It really isn't that amazing.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:33.920
It uses the crest on this coin,
and it's a pretty basic conjuring.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:38.420
Oh, but I can control the movement
of the bubbles to some extent,

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.080
so I guess that part's kind of cool.

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:42.880
So amazing!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:43.920
Is it?

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.630
<b>Express, Ancient Capital No. 7</b>

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.630
<b>For Garm</b>

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.630
<b>First Class, Carriage 1</b>

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.630
I'm so sorry for the trouble.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.080
Oh, it wasn't any trouble at all!

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.500
Come on, let's get on.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.880
Bye!

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.330
Yup, bye-bye!

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:56.460
See you!

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.670
I guess they're going to Garm as well.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.540
Well, we should board, too-

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:04.630
What?

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.790
Hmm? Nothing.

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:09.920
I just thought you showing off
back there was kind of cute.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.040
I wasn't showing off...

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:15.580
You don't have to be embarrassed!

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.670
Keep this up, and you'll regret it.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.920
Ooh, I'm so sorry!

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:26.040
That dang Boobalicious...
Getting all friendly with my Menou!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.170
Wait, isn't that...?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.710
Princess Ashuna!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.170
What are you two doing here?

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:45.330
We came looking for Your Highness, of course!

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:49.830
How could you leave at a time like this,
when His Majesty is dealing with the trial?!

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:54.080
I'm not my father. He can take care of himself.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.250
But I didn't imagine I'd get caught this soon.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.920
Uhhh, she thought she could get away dressed like that?

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.210
That's princess logic for you...

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.170
Come, let's get you back.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:10.130
By the way, what do you think of these bubbles?

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.790
Just a prank, probably?

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.540
It's harmless magecraft.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:16.830
A prank, eh?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.040
Where to?

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:26.170
I'm heading for Garm. That's why I'm here.

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.580
Then we shall accompany you!

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.670
Wow, this is so great.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.750
It really feels like we're off on a journey!

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.710
Isn't this exciting, Menou?!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:47.170
Yes, it is.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.500
Go ahead and enjoy the trip, Akari.

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:59.460
Because when this journey ends, the thing that awaits...

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.290
...is the end of your life.

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Taboo in [Red]</b>

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:39.380
<i>Next episode: Taboo in [Red].</i>
